<article class="env-definition" id="01O0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01O0">Definition <span data-tag="01O0">27.16.7</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\mathcal{A}$ be a quasi-coherent sheaf of graded $\mathcal{O}_ S$-algebras. The <em>relative homogeneous spectrum of $\mathcal{A}$ over $S$</em>, or the <em>homogeneous spectrum of $\mathcal{A}$ over $S$</em>, or the <em>relative Proj of $\mathcal{A}$ over $S$</em> is the scheme constructed in Lemma <a href="/tag/01NQ" data-tag="01NQ">27.15.4</a> which represents the functor $F$ (<a href="/tag/01NX" data-tag="01NX">27.16.4.1</a>), see Lemma <a href="/tag/01NZ" data-tag="01NZ">27.16.6</a>. We denote it $\pi : \underline{\text{Proj}}_ S(\mathcal{A}) \to S$. </p>
